<<<
Go away (& all 2nd-pers. imperatives).
===
*Go away* (& all 2nd-pers. imperatives).
>>>

<<<
Manners be hanged! (& such 3rdpers. curses).
===
*Manners be hanged!* (& such 3rd-pers. curses).
>>>

<<<
Come what may, Be that as it may, Far be it from me to .. ., (& other such stereotyped formulae).
===
*Come what may, Be that as it may, Far be it from me to . . .*, (& other such stereotyped formulae).
>>>

<<<
I shall be 70 come Tuesday.
===
*I shall be 70 come Tuesday.*
>>>

<<<
If he were here now (& all if... were clauses expressing a hypothesis that is not a fact; were & not be, _ & not a fact, are essential).
===
*If he were here now* (& all *if . . . were* clauses expressing a hypothesis that is not a fact; *were* & not *be*, & *not a fact*, are essential).
>>>

<<<
I wish it were over.
===
*I wish it were over.*
>>>

<<<
Though all care be exercised (the difference is still a practical one between Though . . . is,=In spite of the fact that, & Though .. . be,= motive underlying them, Even on the supposition that).
===
*Though all care be exercised* (the difference is still a practical one between *Though . . . is,*=In spite of the fact that, & *Though . . . be,*=Even on the supposition that).
>>>

<<<
What care I how fair she be?
===
*What care I how fair she be?*
>>>

<<<
Lose who may, I still can say...
===
*Lose who may, I still can say . . .*
>>>

<<<
If ladies be but young & fair.
===
*If ladies be but young & fair.*
>>>

<<<
may not resort if it suits them; the - point to be made
===
may not resort if it suits them; the point to be made
>>>

<<<
SURVIVALS In the examples that will be given there is nothing incorrect; the objection to the subjunctives in them is that they diffuse an atmosphere of dullness & formalism over the writing in which they occur; the

& the
===
SURVIVALS

In the examples that will be given there is nothing incorrect; the objection to the subjunctives in them is that they diffuse an atmosphere of dullness & formalism over the writing in which they occur; the motive underlying them, & the
>>>

<<<
+ effect they produce, are the same that attend the choosing of FORMAL WORDS, a reference to which article may save some repetition.
===
+ effect they produce, are the same that attend the choosing of ^^FORMAL WORDS^^, a reference to which article may save some repetition.
>>>

<<<
incoherence. /It is quite obvious
===
incoherence./It is quite obvious
>>>

<<<
decided. /If these others
===
decided./If these others
>>>

<<<
better io leave the sculpture
===
better to leave the sculpture
>>>

<<<
If it have [has] a flaw, that flaw takes the shape of a slight incoherence.
===
*If it have* [has] *a flaw, that flaw takes the shape of a slight incoherence.*
>>>

<<<
It is quite obvious to what grave results such instances as the above may lead, be they [if they are] only sufficiently numerous.
===
*It is quite obvious to what grave results such instances as the above may lead, be they* [if they are] *only sufficiently numerous.*
>>>

<<<
The causes which would probably bring about a protracted civil war in Servia should King Peter die before the question of his successor be [is, or has been] more firmly decided.
===
*The causes which would probably bring about a protracted civil war in Servia should King Peter die before the question of his successor be* [is, or has been] *more firmly decided.*
>>>

<<<
If these others be [are] all we can muster, it were [would be] better to leave the sculpture galleries empty.
===
*If these others be* [are] *all we can muster, it were* [would be] *better to leave the sculpture galleries empty.*
>>>

<<<
If Mr Hobhouse’s analysis of the vices of popular government be [is] correct, much more would seem to be needed.
===
*If Mr Hobhouse's analysis of the vices of popular government be* [is] *correct, much more would seem to be needed.*
>>>

<<<
It were [would be] futile to attempt to deprive it of its real meaning.
===
*It were* [would be] *futile to attempt to deprive it of its real meaning.*
>>>

<<<
Unless immediate action be [is] taken, the country will be so tied that . . .
===
*Unless immediate action be* [is] *taken, the country will be so tied that . . .*
>>>

<<<
That will depend a good deal on whether he be [is] shocked by the cynicism.
===
*That will depend a good deal on whether he be* [is] *shocked by the cynicism.*
>>>

<<<
day:—If that appeal be made & results in the return of the Government to power, then . . ./There are those who, if there be common security
===
day:—*If that appeal* be made & *results in the return of the Government to power, then . . .*/*There are those who, if there* be *common security*
>>>

<<<
& they are all right, not only care nothing for, but would even oppose, the .../If the verdict goes against him his home may be sold up, or if an injunction be obtained against him
===
& *they* are *all right, not only care nothing for, but would even oppose, the . . .*/*If the verdict* goes *against him his home may be sold up, or if an injunction* be obtained *against him*
>>>
